    "title": "Yankees Force Decisive Game 3 in AL Wild Card Series",
    "text": "• Jazz Chisholm Jr. scored the winning run for the New York Yankees in the eighth inning of Game 2 against the Boston Red Sox.\n• The Yankees won the game 4-3, forcing a decisive Game 3 in the AL Wild Card Series.\n• Chisholm made critical defensive plays at second base during the game.\n• Ben Rice hit a two-run homer in the first inning for the Yankees.\n• Aaron Judge contributed with an RBI single.\n• Devin Williams earned the win with a one-hit eighth inning.\n• David Bednar recorded his first postseason save.\n• Trevor Story homered and drove in all three runs for the Red Sox.\n• The Red Sox won Game 1 of the series 3-1.\n• Chisholm made a diving stop to save a run in the seventh inning.\n• The Yankees turned three double plays during the game.\n• Chisholm walked in the eighth inning and scored on Austin Wells' tiebreaking single.\n• Game 3 is scheduled for Thursday night in the Bronx.\n• Cam Schlittler will start for the Yankees in Game 3.\n• Connelly Early will pitch for the Red Sox in place of injured Lucas Giolito.",
